# Commits that only reformat code in place — a Prettier bump, a re-indent.
# GitHub reads this file on its own; locally, run
# `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs` once per clone.
#
# What this can do: for a line a listed commit touched, blame looks for the
# matching line in that commit's parent *in the same file* and credits whoever
# wrote it there. That is right for a reformat, where every line has such a
# twin.
#
# What it cannot do: follow code into another file. A commit that creates a
# file leaves no parent version to look in, so every line keeps its blame on
# the listed commit. And any line the commit genuinely wrote gets pinned on a
# guess — whichever nearby parent line happens to match — which is worse than
# the honest answer.
#
# So a move across files is not listed here. Use `git blame -C -C <file>`,
# which searches the files the commit changed for where each line came from and
# needs no configuration. The split of scripts/ci/repo-rules.mjs into
# scripts/ci/rules/*.mjs (73f4bb8) was listed once and taken out: it did
# nothing for the rule modules or lib.mjs, and in repo-rules.mjs and AGENTS.md
# it credited the new import lines and the rewritten paragraphs to commits that
# never wrote them. `git blame -C -C scripts/ci/rules/env-parity.mjs` takes
# that file from 73 lines on the split to 2.
